    "This proposal CONSTITUTES DEVELOPMENT within the meaning of Section 55 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990, but by virtue of Article 3 and Schedule 2 of the Town and Country (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 and any subsequent legislative amendments is of a class which is described as PERMITTED DEVELOPMENT and therefore planning permission IS NOT REQUIRED subject to the following conditions: \r\n\r\n(a) Solar PV or solar thermal equipment is, so far as practicable, sited so as to minimise its effect on the external appearance of the building; \r\n(b) Solar PV or solar thermal equipment is, so far as practicable, sited so as to minimise its effect on the amenity of the area; and \r\n(c) Solar PV or solar thermal equipment is removed as soon as reasonably practicable when no longer needed."
